// Machine prototypes (work item 0011): entities placed in the world by an
// item, loaded after items.sjson and resolved to a dense Machine_Id.
// item is the item that places the machine; picking the machine up gives
// it back. Each item places at most one machine.
// name_key is a key into data/strings/en.sjson.
// footprint is width (x), depth (z) and height (y) in blocks before
// rotation; a quarter turn swaps width and depth.
// kind selects the panel and the simulation: chest, furnace, capsule,
// belt, inserter, drill, splitter, pipe, offshore_pump, boiler,
// steam_engine, storage_tank, pump, pole, power_switch, lamp, assembler
// or lab.
// The capsule (work item 0013) stands on the landing pad from the start:
// it has no item, cannot be picked up, and holds 8 slots for quest
// rewards and deliveries.
// Chests: slots is the number of item slots.
// Furnaces: fuel_slots, input_slots and output_slots must be 1 each for
// now. speed multiplies the recipe rate (1 is the listed recipe time).
// fuel_power_kilowatts is the power drawn from the fuel while working.
// Belts (work item 0014): belt_shape is flat, ramp or lift (the item
// placed decides the shape; a ramp's up or down and a lift's direction
// are chosen at placement). belt_speed_blocks_per_second is the item speed
// along the belt; it becomes a whole number of 1/256 block units per tick,
// so pick values where speed * 256 / tick rate is an integer (1.875 at
// 60 ticks per second is 8 units).
// Inserters (work item 0015): items_per_minute sets the cycle, which is
// 60 * tick rate / items_per_minute ticks (100 at 36 per minute), half a
// swing to the drop side and half back. A burner inserter has fuel_slots
// = 1 and fuel_power_kilowatts, burned only while the arm moves. Electric
// inserters have electric_power_kilowatts, drawn only while the arm
// moves (work item 0020). filter_slots = 1 makes a filter inserter.
// Drills (work item 0016): placed with at least one footprint cell on a
// vein outcrop, they draw one unit per cycle from the vein's reservoir,
// picked by the vein type's output mix, and drop it into the cell in
// front of their arrow. items_per_minute is the ore rate on a vein whose
// ore share is rate_reference_ore_percent (the iron vein of
// doc/content.md, 80 percent hematite), so the cycle is
// 60 * tick rate * rate_reference_ore_percent / (100 * items_per_minute)
// ticks (192 at 15 per minute and 80 percent), and the spoil comes on top.
// The footprint must be square, so turning a placed drill moves no cell.
// fuel_power_kilowatts is burned only on the ticks the drill works.
// Splitters (work item 0017): stand across two belt cells, so the
// footprint is 1 along the flow (width) and 2 across it (depth);
// belt_speed_blocks_per_second is the speed of items inside it, like the
// belt it joins.
// Fluids (work item 0019, doc/fluids.md): fluid_ports lists a machine's
// ports, each with its own buffer: cell {x, y, z} of the unrotated
// footprint (x along the width, y up, z along the depth), face
// (positive_x, negative_x, positive_y, negative_y, positive_z, negative_z,
// pointing out of the footprint, or "all" for every outward face of the
// footprint), direction (input takes from the network, output gives to
// it, both does either), fluid (optional, a fluids.sjson id the port only
// ever holds) and buffer_litres. Ports turn with the footprint.
// Pipes: buffer_litres per block and flow_litres_per_second, the most a
// connection between two segments moves (1200 is 20 litres per tick).
// Offshore pump: fluid_litres_per_second into its one output port while
// there is room. Placed with the cell in front of its +x end (its intake,
// the end without the port), at its height or one below, a water source.
// Boiler: turns fluid_litres_per_second of its input port's fluid into as
// much of its output port's fluid, burning fuel_power_kilowatts from its
// fuel slot only while it does.
// Steam engine: input ports only. A generator (work item 0020): gives up
// to electric_output_kilowatts to its power network, burning
// fluid_litres_per_second of steam at full output, so a litre of steam is
// electric_output_kilowatts * 1000 / fluid_litres_per_second joules
// (30 kJ), drawn only for the energy delivered.
// Storage tank: one port on every face, its buffer is the tank.
// Pump: moves fluid_litres_per_second from its input to its output port
// whatever the heights, and only with electric_power_kilowatts.
// Power (work item 0020, doc/fluids.md): electric machines (any with
// electric_power_kilowatts: electric inserters, electric drills, pumps,
// lamps) and generators (steam engines) belong to the network of a pole
// whose supply_volume covers one of their cells. A drill without a fuel
// slot and with electric_power_kilowatts is an electric drill.
// Poles: supply_volume is width (x), depth (z) and height (y) of the box
// of cells powered, centred across on the pole (odd width and depth) and
// starting at the pole's bottom. wire_reach connects it to every pole or
// power switch whose origin is at most that far away (straight line, the
// shorter reach of the two counts).
// Power switch: a 1 by 1 by 1 pole without a supply volume that joins the
// networks it wires while on and splits them while off.
// Lamp: electric_power_kilowatts and light_level, the block light it
// gives while its network is satisfied above half.
// Assembler and lab (work item 0021): speed and electric_power_kilowatts,
// no slot fields. An assembler makes recipes with assembler in made_in,
// with one input slot per ingredient and one output slot per product of
// the chosen recipe. A lab has one slot per science pack item any
// technology in technologies.sjson consumes.
